      "id": 1,
      "text": "Albion was first settled by Paul Tenney Peabody in 1833 at the confluence of Kalamazoo River branches, earning the nickname \"The Forks\".",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofalbionmi.gov/residents/city_at_a_glance/history.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The railroad arrived in 1852, prompting Albion’s incorporation as a village in 1855 and sparking industrial growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofalbionmi.gov/residents/city_at_a_glance/history.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1929, the Bohm Theater opened on Christmas Day, becoming a downtown landmark that still hosts performances today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
